tops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":43,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"`work/weights.npz`, `work/NOTES.md` and `work/predictions.json` are written. The controller is untested in simulation, as the rules require.\n\n**What I built:** a queue-scoring controller written directly into the weights. Each phase gets a score in vehicles:\n- vehicles on its stop-line lanes, with left-turn pockets counted ×1.25;\n- halting vehicles upstream, plus 0.25 per moving one;\n- the shared straight-and-left upstream lane split between through and left (halting cars 65% to the left phase);\n- 0.75 extra for the phase that is currently green.\n\nThe network picks the highest score. Layer 1 has 4 units per phase computing the score; layer 2 has 2 near-linear units per phase; the output weight is 8. The other 104 hidden units keep their random starting values. The tuned actuated controller is almost exactly \"most halting vehicles at minimum green\"; my rule agrees with its decisions 82% of the time.\n\n**Trainability (required limits in brackets):**\n\n| measure | value |\n|---|---|\n| median_max_prob | 0.865 (≤ 0.95) |\n| share_max_prob_above_0.99 | 0.168 (≤ 0.30) |\n| max_abs_logit | 8.5 (≤ 15) |\n| sat_l1 / sat_l2 | 0.004 / 0 |\n| dead units | 0 / 0 |\n\n**Checks:** the network's choice matches the rule on 99.2% of recorded states, and on 100% wherever the rule's top two scores differ by at least 0.05 vehicle. That also holds on synthetic congested states with scores up to 69. Probes behave as intended: it holds an empty green, switches for one waiting car, and serves full left pockets.\n\n**Predicted test TTS (veh-h):** low 34.4, nominal 45.0, high 56.8, about ±2. The main risk is under-serving left turns, so pockets overflow and block through traffic, mainly in the high scenario.","ttft_ms":954,"type":"result","duration_ms":1136990,"uuid":"fbc4863b-18d6-4ad3-a30d-6a287ce7c070","ttft_stream_ms":616,"time_to_request_ms":54,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":3,